WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.356
BI Migrations takes you from one analytics platform to another, quickly and accurately.

2
00:00:05.356 --> 00:00:07.080
Ready to watch it in action?

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.734
Your journey is simple.

4
00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:10.942
Scan your estate.

5
00:00:10.942 --> 00:00:12.719
Convert it to open specs.

6
00:00:12.719 --> 00:00:14.851
Build it on your new platform.

7
00:00:14.851 --> 00:00:21.389
We read Domo, Tableau, Power BI and more, and write to Power BI, Superset, Tableau and more.

8
00:00:21.389 --> 00:00:24.160
Today, we will follow Domo to Power BI.

9
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:32.280
It starts in your Dashboard: eleven steps, each completing when something real happens, like a scan or a signature.

10
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.897
Install Estate Scanner on a machine that can reach your platform.

11
00:00:36.897 --> 00:00:39.110
The Dashboard gives you a one-time code.

12
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.305
Type the code in.

13
00:00:41.305 --> 00:00:45.910
The Dashboard knows this copy is yours, and no scan data is sent.

14
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.180
The Dashboard now sees your device.

15
00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.578
Connect your platform.

16
00:00:51.578 --> 00:00:57.280
Domo and Power BI use their own sign-in page, so single sign-on and multi-factor just work.

17
00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.048
Now scan.

18
00:00:59.048 --> 00:01:08.600
Datasets, dataflows, cards, dashboards, calculations, users and every relationship: read-only, into one local file.

19
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.280
Press Sync when you are ready.

20
00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.800
Nothing leaves your machine until you decide.

21
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.740
The scan arrives as a summary of your estate, and your quote is drafted from it.

22
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.368
A person approves the quote.

23
00:01:24.368 --> 00:01:27.250
Accept, sign, and BIMControl is unlocked.

24
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.579
Pair BIMControl the same way.

25
00:01:31.579 --> 00:01:33.490
It runs inside your network.

26
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:42.230
BIMControl rebuilds a dashboard in ten stages: understand it, move the data, build it, publish it, prove it.

27
00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.400
Choose your target: Power BI, or Apache Superset.

28
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.379
Pick a dashboard, and BIMControl shows everything it depends on.

29
00:01:52.379 --> 00:01:53.560
Then press Migrate.

30
00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.999
Watch the ten stages run.

31
00:01:57.999 --> 00:02:01.325
Each saves what it produced, and nothing is guessed.

32
00:02:01.325 --> 00:02:02.860
The report is published.

33
00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.126
Now, proof.

34
00:02:09.126 --> 00:02:16.780
Every Domo card is compared with its new visual, category by category, and every element gets a status and a reason.

35
00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:19.438
Here, most elements match.

36
00:02:19.438 --> 00:02:21.769
Where something differs, you see why.

37
00:02:21.769 --> 00:02:26.180
A difference with a stated reason is a finished result, not a failure.

38
00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.050
And here is your report, live in Power BI, with its semantic model behind it.

39
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:38.160
The evidence and the report return to your Dashboard timeline, then it is handed over to you.

40
00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.719
Scanned, quoted, migrated and proven.

41
00:02:42.719 --> 00:02:44.050
BI Migrations.
